  "title": "# Build: land-merge-queue-first (URGENT, Opus medium; landing job for Landin' Lenny) ## What Brett …",
  "asked": "# Build: land-merge-queue-first (URGENT, Opus medium; landing job for Landin' Lenny) ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) \"You gotta stop merging these one at a time or they're gonna have to run checks again. That's what happened last time.\" ... \"Land the queue first. Stop everything. Stop merging these things one at a time so they don't step on each other's toes. Save the compute.\" Book to **Landin' Lenny**. ## Do, in this order 1. **Pause all one-at-a-time merging NOW**: turn off auto-land (`autoLand.enabled=false` or the land.mjs pause / cron entry) AND auto catch-up (no more merging main into open PRs). Verify nothing merges or re-runs CI except what you do in step 2. Post in the Breakroom chat: 'Auto-merge paused by Brett, landing merge queue first.' 2. **Land ONLY PR #320 (merge-queue)**: update it from main once, fix anything, one CI run, merge, redeploy the console, confirm the queue is live (view + MCP tools `push_banner_mergequeue_*`). Turn on GitHub's native merge queue if available; otherwise use the auto-land stacked mode from #320. 3. **Then put the waiting batch through the queue as ONE stack** (tested once on top of main + everything ahead; failures kicked out, the rest retested only if needed): #327 tab-group-assets, #328 molly-multi-instance-tabs, jump-menu-asset PR, urgent-approval-popup-crash PR, #319 fable-no-approval, axHub pass-dropdowns (axHub repo, separately), #305 terminal-no-focus, #323 app-voice-commands when green, urgent-console-perf when green. Hold back: #318 (red), apps-control-surface (UI Review), and WIP PRs (#299/#301/#302). 4. Leave auto-land OFF afterwards. Only the merge queue merges from now on (update the auto-land settings + RULES.md to say so). 5. **Save compute**: no PR gets updated from main except through the queue, cache GitHub reads (land.mjs was burning ~800 API calls per run), and one deploy per stack, not per PR. 6. Report: what landed, CI runs used, API calls used, anything kicked out and why. Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
